{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nTen ADRs carry operator procedure alongside their decision. `infra/runbooks/` already holds 21 runbooks (`git ls-tree origin/main -- infra/runbooks`). Most procedures already exist there in fuller form; the ADR copies are the drift.\n\n## Approach\n| ADR | Procedural lines (origin/main) | Target | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0012 | `:34-36` bootstrap teardown caution; `:105-108` two-step apply + seven secrets | existing `infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md` §\"Provision from scratch\" (`:88-113`) | add the teardown caution to step 1; replace ADR `:105-108` with `See infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md §\"Provision from scratch\".` |\n| 0048 | `:30-33` import mechanics, `:51-54` state-rm + `RE-HOMED-TO-REBAR.md` marker, `:68-70` operator follow-ups | existing `infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md`, new section `## Re-homing mechanics (from ADR 0048)` placed before `## Secrets` (`:67`) | move; ADR keeps decision clauses 1–6 as one sentence each + pointer |\n| 0079 | `:61-65` Back-out incl. \"units ship DISABLED; enable after a manual dry-run\" | existing `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` §\"Continuous auto-deploy (epic 88ab / story 8903)\" (`:522`), whose `**Back-out (disable auto-deploy):**` paragraph is at `:563` | add the ship-disabled/dry-run sentence there; ADR `## Back-out` body → pointer. Amendments (`:74-128`) stay (rationale). |\n| 0085 | `:58-71` eventual-consistency discipline, `:73-79` report procedure | NEW `infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md` (how to run `scripts/run_live_matrix.py`, `pytest -m live`, env vars, report paths, index-lag rules, leak log) | move; ADR keeps §1–§2 + pointer. Also fix `scripts/run_live_matrix.py:2` docstring \"ADR 0037 §4\" → \"ADR 0085 (archived into ADR 0121 §20); runbook infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md\". |\n| 0031 | `:158-165` Operator break-glass (clear a wedged `refs/reconciler/lock`) | existing `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` §\"The reconciler cursor\" (`:252`) | move the two commands; ADR keeps pointer (the only procedure inside the consolidation set). CORRECTED from `:158-168`, which ran 3 lines past the section and swallowed the `## Lease self-healing` heading at `:167`; `:166` is blank. |\n| 0105 | `:94-97` \"A one-time operator cutover is required… Until that runs…\" | existing `infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md` §REMEDIATE (`:140-185`) already holds the procedure | replace the bullet with `The one-time cutover ran — task gnarly-sinistrous-groundhog (097b-de23-bf12-4c38); procedure and scrub: infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md §REMEDIATE.` |\n| 0109 | `:112-123` tier-selection table (already single-sourced at `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Validating a gate change: which replay tier\"), `:125-139` cost table | NEW `infra/runbooks/plan-review-eval-ops.md` §\"Replay tiers: invocation and budget\" (`python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0|tier1|tier2 …`, cost table, cap/ledger) | move cost table; replace §6 table with pointer to the gate doc; keep §6's \"required, not advisory\" sentence and the `plan-review-eval:` trailer convention |\n| 0113 | `:85-93` change-triggered execution (`eval-changed-rubrics` job, `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml:41`), `:95-109` heal-loop schedule + `unreliable-criterion:` ticket handling | same NEW `infra/runbooks/plan-review-eval-ops.md` §\"Heal loop and the unreliable-criterion breaker\" (`rebar criteria heal [--dry-run]`, ledger `.rebar/fixture_heal_ledger.jsonl`, how a human resolves a breaker ticket) | move the operating steps; ADR keeps decisions 6–7 as rules + pointer |\n| 0112 | `:241-252` Open items (all resolved: S1–S6 children of epic `6202-e1c7-c57f-4897` closed; cap procedures at `review-bot-ops.md:876,1008,1127,1240` — the four `## … (ADR 0112 / story …)` sections — and `gate-scratch-mount.md`) | existing runbooks (no new text) | replace `## Open items` with `## Open items — resolved` naming the closing story per item and the runbook sections; keep Decisions 1–7 verbatim (cited by number from `infra/scripts/*.sh`, `provision-restore.md:126`, `review-bot-ops.md:739`, `infra/terraform/main.tf:43`; `docs/config.md:657,676` name the ADR but no decision number) |\n| 0059 | `:613-633` §8 Bedrock model-id trap set; `:666-693` §10 compose line anchors and the \"read d2ce before quoting\" status | existing `infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md` §\"Which model id to use\" (`:133`) gets the trap list; `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` §\"Kill-switch: revert the LLM path from Bedrock to direct Anthropic\" (`:374`) gets the current-wiring paragraph | move; ADR keeps one-sentence findings + pointers. Write \"the removed `REBAR_LLM_MODEL`\" in the runbook (`tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_removal.py:115-150` scans `review-bot-ops.md` for removal context). §9 and \"Evidence-hygiene rules\" stay (findings, not procedure). |\n\nCurrent vocabulary only (`bridge status`, never `bridge-status`) in new runbook text **and in every line this story MOVES**: the stale-vocabulary scan's `_HISTORY_PREFIXES` exempts `docs/adr/` but not `infra/runbooks/`, so prose unscanned inside an ADR becomes scanned on arrival. Update any legacy spelling as part of the move. Cite modules/CLI, never `docs/experiments/...` paths (eval-harness epic moves them).\n\n## Scope\nEdit ADRs: `docs/adr/0012-iac-foundations.md`, `0031-reconciler-ref-lock.md`, `0048-rehome-snap-shared-infra.md`, `0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md`, `0079-autodeploy-on-box-timer.md`, `0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md`, `0105-ssm-secrets-never-in-terraform-state.md`, `0109-plan-review-replay-harness.md`, `0112-on-box-disk-ceiling-architecture.md`, `0113-fixture-mining-and-admission-protocol.md`. Edit runbooks: `infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md`, `sso-auth-host.md`, `review-bot-ops.md`, `ssm-secret-write-only.md`, `bedrock-access.md`. New: `infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md`, `infra/runbooks/plan-review-eval-ops.md`. Also `scripts/run_live_matrix.py` (docstring).\n\n## Testing\n`python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` (runbook links resolve); `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`; `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check`; `python scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py`; `pytest tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_removal.py::test_no_prose_doc_advertises_the_variable_as_live tests/unit/test_plan_review_docs.py tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py`; then SEPARATELY `pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/ -k bridge_vocabulary_stale` (`-k` filters the whole run, so folding it in would deselect the modules above; the selector survives story `b721-6c6d-504e-45da`, which renames that module in place to `test_bridge_vocabulary_stale.py` with no ordering link between the two stories); `ruff check scripts/run_live_matrix.py`.\n\n**ADR 0031 and 0085 line numbers shift by +2 when story S3 (`8257-3a28`) lands.** They are the table's only rows inside S3's 20-ADR set; S3 inserts a two-line archive banner above each body. Measured against S3's tree: 0031 Operator break-glass `:160-167`; 0085 §3 `:60-73`, §4 `:75-81` (the pre-S3 `:158-165`, `:58-71`, `:73-79` in the table). Confirm by content before editing — locate the `### Operator break-glass`, `### 3. Eventual-consistency discipline for live probes` and `### 4. Report` headings, each section running to the line before the next `#` heading. The other 7 ADRs (0012, 0048, 0059, 0079, 0105, 0109, 0113) are outside S3's set; all their cites, and every runbook anchor in the table, were re-verified against `origin/main` b127d403836.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] For each of the ten listed ADRs, `grep -c 'infra/runbooks/' docs/adr/<file>` ≥ 1 and the moved line ranges above no longer appear (`git diff -U0` shows them removed).\n- [x] The two new runbooks exist and every `](…)` in them resolves (`check_docs_index.py --check` exit 0).\n- [x] `grep -n 'ADR 0037' scripts/run_live_matrix.py` is empty; `grep -n 'Open items$' docs/adr/0112-*.md` is empty."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793528535530750001,"uuid":"fb12bb98-a687-4fbe-86ae-5b04cbb9c070"}